---
title: Erosion by aggregation
---
Fire particles at a finished map and let them eat at its walls, so it looks more organic and keeps its structure [[t:191-197 s:21]].

## The rule
1. Start from a finished map. The demo’s: random rooms joined by corridors [[c08:21-83]].
2. **Repeat 500 times** [[c08:86]]:
   1. start a particle on a random open tile [[c08:92-101]];
   2. step it at random until it stands on rock [[c08:102-125]];
   3. dig that tile of rock [[c08:102-128]].

- **One tile a particle:** the first rock its walk reaches from inside the open area [[c08:86-128]].

## Step through it
@@steps limit=5 mid=1

## Controls
@@control iterations
Particles fired, each digging one tile [[c08:86-128]].

## What it produces, measured
@@measured

- **Talk says:** the map becomes more and more organic looking, while keeping its basic structure [[t:196-197]].
- **Floor share:** 500 particles lift it from random rooms’ {{c01.floor_share.median}} to {{c08.floor_share.median}} [[run:c01.floor_share.median c08.floor_share.median]].
- **Dead ends:** from {{c01.dead_ends.max}} on every seed to {{c08.dead_ends.median}} at the median [[run:c01.dead_ends.max c08.dead_ends.median]].
- **Still one piece:** {{c08.regions.max}} region on every seed [[run:c08.regions.max]].
  - **Why:** erosion only opens tiles next to open ones [[own]].

## Where it fails
@@fails

- **No cap in the talk’s code:** a particle’s walk runs until it reaches rock [[c08:100-128]].
- **Ours has a cap:** {{c08.fails.guard-hit}} of these seeds reach it [[run:c08.fails.guard-hit]].

